--- !u!114 &781807682
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 781807678}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 868b69d30c1ad2f43be00d8c6eac179d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _textObject: {fileID: 2057283383}
  _disclaimer:
  - Press <color=green>Left Mouse Button [LMB]</color> or the <color=green>Enter
    Key</color> to view the project disclaimer. These inputs must be used to navigate
    through each consecutive description.
  - "You are being invited to take part in a research study.  Before you decide,
    it is important for you to understand why the research is being done and what
    it will involve.  Please take time to read the following information carefully
    and discuss it with others if you wish.  Ask us if there is anything that is
    not clear or if you would like more information.  Take time to decide whether
    you wish to take part. \n\n<b>What is the purpose of the study?</b>\r\nGamification
    of education provides an effective medium in teaching educational concepts including
    mathematics and physics. Project Polynomial will evaluate the effectiveness of
    gamification and provide thorough research and statistics on the impact it has
    on students within a generic educational setting. \nThis study discovers the
    benefits and drawbacks of pedagogical methods through gamifying mathematical
    concepts. The core aim is to provide a bespoke, yet educational gaming experience
    for users, such that information acquired through the project will be retained
    surpassing traditional educational means."
  - '<b>Why have I been chosen?</b>

    You have selected as a participant as you
    are a legal adult that has access to a computer that can run the project. Your
    computer will let you submit information more effectively, compared to mobile
    devices. Additionally, you have a GCSE level (or equivalent) of understanding
    with core mathematics. A basic understanding of mathematics is required, however
    you fit the criteria for this project.


    <b>Do I have to take part?</b>

    It
    is up to you to decide whether to take part.  If you decide to take part, you
    will be given this information sheet to keep and be asked to sign a consent form. 
    If you decide to take part, you are still free to withdraw at any time and without
    giving a reason.  A decision to withdraw at any time, or a decision not to take
    part, will not affect you in any way.

'
  - "<b>What will happen to me if I take part?</b>\r\nThere will be two sessions
    lasting at maximum 30 minutes, these sessions can be in person or online through
    a Microsoft Teams call. \n\nIn the first session, the participant will be informally
    taught advanced mathematical concepts related to algebra (polynomials and complex
    numbers). After a 15-minute educational session, the participant will then answer
    a multiple-choice questionnaire, testing their knowledge on the information recently
    acquired. The answers and time taken to complete each question will be saved
    for further analysis. Subsequently, the participant will detail personal preferences,
    relating to how they found the material provided.\n\nIn the second session, the
    participant has complete access to the \u201CProject Polynomial\u201D project
    demo and will be tasked to complete the game in its entirety. This game will
    take no longer than 20 minutes to complete. This project will test you with the
    mathematic concepts related to algebra (polynomials and complex numbers). Additionally,
    the project will automatically monitor how fast and well the participant has
    answered the questions in every aspect of the game. The participant\u2019s performance
    will be documented; regarding how well they grasped the game mechanics. Lastly,
    the participant will fill out a questionnaire detailing their experience with
    the project.\r\nAll personal information will be discarded as no-one will be
    identifiable in the final report."
  - "<b>What are the possible disadvantages and risks of taking part?</b>\r\nThere
    are no disadvantages or risks foreseen in taking part in the study.\n\n<b>What
    are the possible benefits of taking part?</b>\r\nBy taking part, you will be
    contributing to the development of the test towards games that are tailored towards
    educational subjects. \n\n<b>What if something goes wrong?</b>\r\nIf you wish
    to complain or have any concerns about any aspect of the way you have been approached
    or treated during the course of this study, please contact <color=yellow>Dr,
    Silvester Czanner, Head of the School of Computer and Engineering Sciences, </color>University
    of Chester (s.czanner@chester.ac.uk).\r\n\r\n"
  - "<b>Will my taking part in the study be kept confidential?</b>\r\nAll information
    which is collected about you during the research will be kept strictly confidential
    so that only the researcher carrying out the research will have access to such
    information.  \n\n<b>What will happen to the results of the research study?</b>\r\nThe
    results will be written up into a dissertation for my final project of my Computer
    Science BCS Honours degree. Individuals who participate will not be identified
    in any subsequent report or publication.\n\n<b>Who is organising the research?</b>\r\nThe
    research is conducted as part of an innovation project within The School of Computer
    and Engineering Sciences at the University of Chester. <color=yellow>The study
    is organised with supervision from the department, by Ralph Ferneyhough (r.ferneyhough@chester.ac.uk).</color>"
  - "<b>Who may I contact for further information?</b>\r\nIf you would like more
    information about the research before you decide whether you would be willing
    to take part, please contact:\r\n<color=yellow>Ibrahim Anjorin : 2113691@chester.ac.uk</color>\n\n<b>Retention
    and publication of participant\u2019s data</b>\r\nParticipants should note that
    data collected from this project may be retained and published in an anonymised
    form. By agreeing to participate in this project, you are consenting to the retention
    and publication of data."
  - Thank you for your interest in this research.
